Feature: Survey grids and distances
  To make a map of an area, draw a polygon around it. The planner fills the polygon with
  parallel lines of waypoints at the plan altitude. The distance between the lines suits the
  camera. In Mission Planner, this is Auto WP, Grid. As in Mission Planner, the grid cannot
  have holes. If the polygon has the shape of a U, the plane also flies over the open middle.

  The cursor readout always shows the range and bearing from home. To find the distance
  between two points, measure from one point to the other. The map shows the distance.

  Expectation: A survey grid fills the area with waypoints
    Given the map tool is PLAN
    And the plan has 0 items
    When the operator draws a survey grid
    Then the plan has at least 4 items
    And the last plan item is WAYPOINT

  Expectation: Measuring between two points shows the distance
    When the operator measures between two points
    Then the measured distance is shown
